                    <ol>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Emotional Stability:</b>
                            People low in neuroticism tend to be emotionally
                            stable and resilient in the face of life's
                            challenges. They are less prone to experiencing
                            intense negative emotions such as anxiety,
                            worry, and fear, even in stressful
                            situations.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Optimism:</b> Individuals
                            low in neuroticism often have a positive outlook
                            on life. They tend to approach challenges with a
                            sense of optimism and confidence, believing in
                            their ability to overcome obstacles and adapt to
                            changing circumstances.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Calmness and Composure:</b>
                            Low neuroticism individuals typically maintain a
                            sense of calmness and composure even in the
                            midst of adversity. They are able to keep their
                            emotions in check and respond to stressful
                            situations in a rational and level-headed
                            manner.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Resilience:</b> People low
                            in neuroticism possess a strong sense of
                            resilience and inner strength. They are able to
                            bounce back quickly from setbacks and
                            disappointments, viewing them as temporary
                            setbacks rather than insurmountable
                            obstacles.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Steadiness in
