                            relationships with others. They are less likely
                            to engage in conflict or drama and are able to
                            maintain a sense of equilibrium and harmony in
                            their interpersonal interactions.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Positive Self-Image:</b>
                            Individuals low in neuroticism generally have a
                            positive self-image and high self-esteem. They
                            are comfortable in their own skin and have a
                            healthy sense of self-worth and
                            self-assurance.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Adaptive Coping
                                Strategies:</b> Low neuroticism individuals
                            are adept at using adaptive coping strategies to
                            manage stress and adversity. They may engage in
                            problem-solving, seek social support, or
                            practice relaxation techniques to alleviate
                            stress and promote well-being.</li>
                        <li class="list-item"><b>Focus on the Present:</b>
                            People low in neuroticism tend to focus more on
                            the present moment rather than dwelling on past
                            regrets or worrying excessively about the
                            future. They are able to savor life's simple
                            pleasures and find joy in the present
                            moment.</li>
