                        consistently across different situations and
                        contexts.
                        These patterns provide a framework for understanding
                        how
                        various personality traits interact and influence
                        behavior, cognition, and emotion.<br />
                        One way to visualize personality patterns is through
                        the
                        use of a circumplex graph. A circumplex graph is a
                        circular diagram that represents the
                        interrelationships
                        among different personality traits based on their
                        proximity to one another on the circle.<br />
                        By plotting various personality traits on the
                        circumplex
                        graph, we can identify specific personality patterns
                        or
                        profiles that capture the configuration of traits
                        exhibited by individuals.<br />
                        Each circumplex has four sections, with each section
                        describing a typical pattern. The area of each
                        section
                        shows how well that pattern describes you. A larger
                        area
                        indicates a better fit for that pattern.<br />
                        Some of your circumplex graphs will show a clear
                        preference for one pattern. Others will show a more
                        even
                        spread across two or three patterns. Where you have
                        nearly equal scores for two or three patterns you
                        can
                        expect that both or all three patterns describe you
                        equally well.

